From f0146e0000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH 0146e] evergo: task_coalition_get_thread_group must never return NULL

0145e fixed thread_group_init_thread() so a thread is not BORN with a NULL
thread_group.  The v71 boot (k5c09b004) still dies in the very same
thread_group.c:171 assertion, which means the NULL is written back later,
during the thread's life.

The real source is one function:

    struct thread_group *
    task_coalition_get_thread_group(task_t task)
    {
        coalition_t coal = task->coalition[COALITION_TYPE_JETSAM];
        if (coal == COALITION_NULL)
            return init_coalition[JETSAM]->j.thread_group;
        return coal->j.thread_group;        /* <-- NULL while being torn down */
    }

coalition.c:980 sets coal->j.thread_group = NULL when a jetsam coalition is
reaped.  Every caller of this function assumes the result is valid:

  thread_group.c:644  thread_group_get_home_group() -> first candidate for
                      thread_compute_resolved_thread_group(), whose result is
                      assigned straight to t->thread_group (lines 781/1140)
  bank.c:942          thread_group_retain(task_coalition_get_thread_group(task))
  coalition.c:1607..  thread_group_set_flags_locked(...)

Fix it once at the source: if coal->j.thread_group is NULL, return the
init jetsam coalition's group - the exact same fallback the function already
uses for COALITION_NULL (coalition.c:1555).  That group is created at boot
and never released, so no retain is needed.

This makes 0145e's birth-time guard redundant but harmless (defence in depth),
and it covers the run-time hierarchy resolution that 0145e could not reach.
Report once per distinct task so a genuinely broken coalition stays visible.
---
diff --git a/osfmk/kern/coalition.c b/osfmk/kern/coalition.c
index 10bd5e7..6299f29 100644
--- a/osfmk/kern/coalition.c
+++ b/osfmk/kern/coalition.c
@@ -1554,6 +1554,27 @@ task_coalition_get_thread_group(task_t task)
 	if (coal == COALITION_NULL) {
 		return init_coalition[COALITION_TYPE_JETSAM]->j.thread_group;
 	}
+#if defined(SWEET)
+	/*
+	 * evergo (0146e): coalition.c sets coal->j.thread_group to NULL when a
+	 * jetsam coalition is reaped, while the task still points at it.  The
+	 * v70/v71 boots died in sched_clutch_for_thread() because
+	 * thread_group_get_home_group() -> thread_compute_resolved_thread_group()
+	 * fed that NULL straight back into t->thread_group at run time.
+	 *
+	 * Fall back to the init jetsam coalition's group - the same one used
+	 * above for COALITION_NULL - which lives for the whole boot.
+	 */
+	if (__improbable(coal->j.thread_group == NULL)) {
+		static task_t last_task;
+		if (last_task != task) {
+			last_task = task;
+			printf("SWEET COAL: task %p coalition %p has no thread "
+			    "group, using init jetsam group\n", task, coal);
+		}
+		return init_coalition[COALITION_TYPE_JETSAM]->j.thread_group;
+	}
+#endif
 	return coal->j.thread_group;
 }
 
